{"openapi":"3.1.0","info":{"title":"UniTrack API","description":"Hub API for the UniTrack bus ticketing & live-tracking platform.","version":"0.1.0"},"paths":{"/health":{"get":{"tags":["meta"],"summary":"Health","operationId":"health_health_get","responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"additionalProperties":{"type":"string"},"type":"object","title":"Response Health Health Get"}}}}}}},"/auth/register/student":{"post":{"tags":["auth"],"summary":"Register Student","operationId":"register_student_auth_register_student_post","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/StudentRegister"}}},"required":true},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/UserOut"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/auth/register/helper":{"post":{"tags":["auth"],"summary":"Register Helper","operationId":"register_helper_auth_register_helper_post","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HelperRegister"}}},"required":true},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/UserOut"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/auth/verify-email":{"get":{"tags":["auth"],"summary":"Verify Email","operationId":"verify_email_auth_verify_email_get","parameters":[{"name":"token","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","title":"Token"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/UserOut"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/auth/login":{"post":{"tags":["auth"],"summary":"Login","operationId":"login_auth_login_post","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/LoginRequest"}}},"required":true},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/TokenPair"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/auth/refresh":{"post":{"tags":["auth"],"summary":"Refresh","description":"Exchange a refresh token for a new pair, invalidating the one presented.\n\nRotation matters: without it every refresh token ever issued stays usable\nfor its full 30 days, so a single leaked token is a month of silent access\nthat no logout can end. Here the presented token is denied-listed as part of\nthe exchange, which also means replaying an old one is *detectable* — and a\nreplay is either a stolen token or a broken client, never normal traffic.\n\nRotation is softened by a short grace window, because \"never normal traffic\"\nis not quite true for this app: the helper's UI and its GPS service isolate\nhold the same refresh token and reach 15-minute expiry together, so they\nlegitimately refresh at the same instant. See `claim_rotation` for how both\nend up with the same pair instead of one of them being signed out mid-trip.","operationId":"refresh_auth_refresh_post","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/RefreshRequest"}}},"required":true},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/TokenPair"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/auth/logout":{"post":{"tags":["auth"],"summary":"Logout","description":"End this session: deny-list the access token and the refresh token.\n\nDeleting tokens client-side was never logout — the tokens stayed valid on\nany device that had copied them. Revoking the refresh token is the part that\nmatters, since it is the one worth 30 days.\n\nA refresh token belonging to a *different* user is ignored rather than\nrevoked, so this cannot be used to sign other people out.","operationId":"logout_auth_logout_post","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/LogoutRequest"}}},"required":true},"responses":{"204":{"description":"Successful Response"},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}},"security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}]}},"/auth/me":{"get":{"tags":["auth"],"summary":"Me","operationId":"me_auth_me_get","responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/UserOut"}}}}},"security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}]}},"/admin/helpers":{"get":{"tags":["admin"],"summary":"List Helpers","description":"List helper accounts — the admin panel's approval queue.\n\nNote there is no auth code in this handler. The router guard already ran;\nby the time we are here the caller is a known, active admin.","operationId":"list_helpers_admin_helpers_get","security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"helper_status","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HelperStatus"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Filter by approval state; omit for all.","title":"Helper Status"},"description":"Filter by approval state; omit for all."}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HelperOut"},"title":"Response List Helpers Admin Helpers Get"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed or expired access token"},"403":{"description":"Authenticated, but not an admin"},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/admin/helpers/{helper_id}/approve":{"post":{"tags":["admin"],"summary":"Approve Helper","description":"Approve a pending helper so they can start sending GPS (spec §8).","operationId":"approve_helper_admin_helpers__helper_id__approve_post","security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"helper_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","title":"Helper Id"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HelperOut"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed or expired access token"},"403":{"description":"Authenticated, but not an admin"},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/admin/users/{user_id}/suspend":{"post":{"tags":["admin"],"summary":"Suspend User","description":"Suspend an account. Takes effect on the caller's very next request.\n\nImmediate revocation is exactly what RULE 3 buys. A suspended user's access\ntoken is still cryptographically valid and unexpired — nothing can un-issue\nit. What stops them is `get_principal` reading a fresh snapshot that says\n`suspended` and raising 401. Skip the invalidation and that check reads a\nstale snapshot instead, so a suspended account keeps its access.","operationId":"suspend_user_admin_users__user_id__suspend_post","security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"user_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","title":"User Id"}}],"responses":{"204":{"description":"Successful Response"},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed or expired access token"},"403":{"description":"Authenticated, but not an admin"},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/admin/alerts":{"get":{"tags":["admin"],"summary":"List Alerts","description":"The emergency console's list — worst first, newest first within severity.\n\nBacked by `ix_alerts_status_severity`, so the default view stays an index\nscan over open rows rather than a sort of the whole table as history grows.","operationId":"list_alerts_admin_alerts_get","security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"alert_status","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AlertStatus"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Defaults to open; pass null for all.","default":"open","title":"Alert Status"},"description":"Defaults to open; pass null for all."},{"name":"limit","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"integer","maximum":200,"minimum":1,"default":50,"title":"Limit"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AlertOut"},"title":"Response List Alerts Admin Alerts Get"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed or expired access token"},"403":{"description":"Authenticated, but not an admin"},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/admin/alerts/{alert_id}/acknowledge":{"post":{"tags":["admin"],"summary":"Acknowledge Alert","description":"Claim an alert so two admins do not work the same incident.","operationId":"acknowledge_alert_admin_alerts__alert_id__acknowledge_post","security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"alert_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","title":"Alert Id"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AlertOut"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed or expired access token"},"403":{"description":"Authenticated, but not an admin"},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/admin/alerts/{alert_id}/resolve":{"post":{"tags":["admin"],"summary":"Resolve Alert","description":"Close an incident. A resolved alert keeps who acknowledged it and why.","operationId":"resolve_alert_admin_alerts__alert_id__resolve_post","security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"alert_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","title":"Alert Id"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AlertResolveIn"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AlertOut"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed or expired access token"},"403":{"description":"Authenticated, but not an admin"},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/admin/buses":{"post":{"tags":["admin"],"summary":"Create Bus","description":"Create a new bus in the fleet.","operationId":"create_bus_admin_buses_post","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BusCreate"}}},"required":true},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BusOut"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed or expired access token"},"403":{"description":"Authenticated, but not an admin"},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}},"security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}]}},"/admin/buses/list":{"post":{"tags":["admin"],"summary":"Create Bus List","description":"Create multiple buses at once (batch creation).","operationId":"create_bus_list_admin_buses_list_post","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BusListCreate"}}},"required":true},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BusOut"},"type":"array","title":"Response Create Bus List Admin Buses List Post"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed or expired access token"},"403":{"description":"Authenticated, but not an admin"},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}},"security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}]}},"/admin/buses/batch":{"post":{"tags":["admin"],"summary":"Create Bus List","description":"Create multiple buses at once (batch creation).","operationId":"create_bus_list_admin_buses_batch_post","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BusListCreate"}}},"required":true},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BusOut"},"type":"array","title":"Response Create Bus List Admin Buses Batch Post"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed or expired access token"},"403":{"description":"Authenticated, but not an admin"},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}},"security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}]}},"/fleet/buses":{"get":{"tags":["fleet"],"summary":"List Buses","description":"The bus picker in the helper app.\n\nReplaces typing a UUID by hand, which was the previous state of affairs and\nis exactly as error-prone as it sounds.","operationId":"list_buses_fleet_buses_get","security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"only_active","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"boolean","description":"Hide inactive/maintenance buses.","default":true,"title":"Only Active"},"description":"Hide inactive/maintenance buses."}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BusOut"},"title":"Response List Buses Fleet Buses Get"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/fleet/routes":{"get":{"tags":["fleet"],"summary":"List Routes","operationId":"list_routes_fleet_routes_get","security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"only_active","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"boolean","default":true,"title":"Only Active"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/RouteOut"},"title":"Response List Routes Fleet Routes Get"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/fleet/routes/{route_id}":{"get":{"tags":["fleet"],"summary":"Get Route","description":"One route with its ordered stops — what the map draws.\n\n`selectinload` fetches route_stops and their stops in two extra queries\nrather than one per stop. The lazy default would issue an N+1 storm on a\nroute with thirty stops, on an endpoint every map load hits.","operationId":"get_route_fleet_routes__route_id__get","security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"route_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","title":"Route Id"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/RouteDetailOut"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}},"/fleet/stops":{"get":{"tags":["fleet"],"summary":"List Stops","operationId":"list_stops_fleet_stops_get","responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/StopOut"},"type":"array","title":"Response List Stops Fleet Stops Get"}}}}},"security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}]}},"/helper/trips/start":{"post":{"tags":["helper"],"summary":"Start Trip","description":"Begin a trip. Everything the bus produces from now on binds to it.","operationId":"start_trip_helper_trips_start_post","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/TripStartRequest"}}},"required":true},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/TripOut"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}},"security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}]}},"/helper/trips/end":{"post":{"tags":["helper"],"summary":"End Trip","description":"Close the caller's live trip.\n\nNo trip id in the path: a helper has at most one live trip, enforced by a\npartial unique index, so there is nothing to disambiguate — and no id for a\nclient to get wrong or forge.","operationId":"end_trip_helper_trips_end_post","responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/TripOut"}}}}},"security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}]}},"/helper/trips/active":{"get":{"tags":["helper"],"summary":"Get Active Trip","description":"What the app calls on launch to recover state after a restart or crash.","operationId":"get_active_trip_helper_trips_active_get","responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ActiveTripOut"},{"type":"null"}],"title":"Response Get Active Trip Helper Trips Active Get"}}}}},"security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}]}},"/helper/seats":{"post":{"tags":["helper"],"summary":"Report Seats","description":"Report how full the bus is (spec §6 `seat_reports`).\n\nRequires a live trip: an occupancy count with no trip cannot be attributed\nto a route or a time window, which is the only thing that makes it useful.","operationId":"report_seats_helper_seats_post","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SeatReportIn"}}},"required":true},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SeatStateOut"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}},"security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}]}},"/helper/alerts":{"post":{"tags":["helper"],"summary":"Raise Alert","description":"Raise an alert from the emergency screen (spec §7.6).\n\nWorks without a live trip on purpose — a breakdown on the way to the depot\nis still a breakdown, and an SOS must never be refused on a technicality.\n\nSeverity is assigned by the server from the type; the client does not get a\nsay, or every alert would arrive critical.","operationId":"raise_alert_helper_alerts_post","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AlertRaiseIn"}}},"required":true},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AlertOut"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}},"security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}]}},"/helper/gps":{"post":{"tags":["helper"],"summary":"Ingest Gps","description":"Receive a batch of GPS fixes from a helper device (spec §7.3).\n\nWrites the newest fix to `bus:{id}:pos` (TTL 60 s) for \"where is bus 7 right\nnow\", publishes to the fleet channel for the admin live map, and XADDs every\nfix to the `gps_ingest` stream. The worker drains that stream into\nElasticsearch.\n\nTrip binding\n------------\nIf the helper has a live trip, its id rides along on every fix and the\ntrip's bus wins over whatever the client sent — the server decides which bus\na helper is driving, not the phone.\n\nFixes with no live trip are still accepted, with an empty `trip_id`. That is\na **transition allowance** for the current helper build, which has no trip\nUI yet; it is why `trip_id` is nullable downstream. Once the app ships trip\nlifecycle, make this a 409 and delete this paragraph.","operationId":"ingest_gps_helper_gps_post","requestBody":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/GpsBatch"}}},"required":true},"responses":{"202":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/GpsAccepted"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}},"security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}]}},"/track/nearby":{"get":{"tags":["tracking"],"summary":"Nearby Buses","description":"Buses with a recent fix within `radius_km`, closest first.\n\n`collapse` on bus_id returns one hit per bus; the `_geo_distance` sort makes\nthat hit the closest point and exposes its distance.","operationId":"nearby_buses_track_nearby_get","security":[{"HTTPBearer":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"lat","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"number","maximum":90,"minimum":-90,"title":"Lat"}},{"name":"lng","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"number","maximum":180,"minimum":-180,"title":"Lng"}},{"name":"radius_km","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"number","maximum":50,"exclusiveMinimum":0,"default":5,"title":"Radius Km"}},{"name":"limit","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"integer","maximum":100,"minimum":1,"default":20,"title":"Limit"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"title":"Response Nearby Buses Track Nearby Get"}}}},"422":{"description":"Validation Error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}}},"components":{"schemas":{"ActiveTripOut":{"properties":{"trip_id":{"type":"s